{
  "_comment": [
    "Capabilities whose existence in code and description in the docs must not drift apart.",
    "",
    "This file exists because they did, four times in one session: README carried no mention",
    "of mirror mode, seals, NIS2 or DORA while the sales offer led with the first and two",
    "sessions of work had gone into the rest (#73); ROADMAP listed the mirror as 4-8 weeks of",
    "unstarted work after it had shipped, and its P1 table contradicted its own phase tables",
    "(#73, #74); the release checklist listed the mirror as open for the same reason (#75).",
    "",
    "Every one was found by a human reading two documents side by side and noticing. That is",
    "not a control. scripts/check-doc-drift.py is.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  name        - what it is called in conversation",
    "  proof       - {file, contains}: the thing in the CODE that settles whether it exists",
    "  keywords    - how the docs refer to it; any one counts as a mention",
    "  must_mention- documents that would be lying by omission without it",
    "",
    "Add a capability here when it becomes something a buyer or an operator is told about."
